    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n77702" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παν-ῠπέρτατος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">η</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>highest of all</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μεγέθει π.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>Mu.</u>
					397a15
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. ἐρρίζωνται</span>, of trees,
			are rooted <i>highest</i> on the mountain, <i><span class="en">
				A.R.
				1.1122
			</span></i>: hence, <i>most remote</i> or <i>farthest from land</i>,
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. εἰν ἁλὶ κεῖται</span>, of
			Ithaca, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				9.25
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>supreme</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Call.
				<u>Jov.</u>
				91
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Orph.
				<u>H.</u>
				19.2
			</span></i>,al.</div>
